  "worked_solution": "This is a rational function, so it is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we start by factoring the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-1}{x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x-1)({x}^{2}+x+1)}{x-1} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+x+1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $x\\ne 1.$\n\nThis function is continuous everywhere except at the excluded point $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the domain consists of the union of the intervals $(-\\infty ,1)$ and $(1,\\infty ),$ namely\n\n$$\n(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty )\n$$\n\nand the function is also continuous on this union of intervals.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
